# RxJS operators

## Higher-order mapping

| Goal | Operator |
|------|----------|
| Latest only; cancel stale | `switchMap` |
| Parallel / all inners | `mergeMap` |
| Serial ordered | `concatMap` |
| Ignore while busy | `exhaustMap` |

## Pipe design

- Read left-to-right: normalize → filter → time → flatten → present.
- Pure transforms in `map`/`filter`; side effects only in `tap` (sparingly).
- Put `catchError` **on the inner** when the outer must keep going.
- `reduce` / `toArray` / `forkJoin` need **completion**; do not use on infinite streams without `take*`.
- Prefer `share` / `shareReplay({ bufferSize, refCount: true })` over hand-rolled `multicast` unless you need manual `connect()`.

```js
// ✅ typeahead
input$.pipe(
  debounceTime(300),
  distinctUntilChanged(),
  switchMap((q) => search(q).pipe(catchError(() => of([])))),
);
```
